      "omega-python publishes a call's first three arguments and its last as text, so an extension's name and its sources argument as written are stated; it does not publish the elements of a list argument, so the individual C++ files in sources=['a.cpp', 'b.cu'] are not separate facts and the edge from an extension module to each C++ file it compiles is reported as not found. The same limit hides include_dirs, extra_compile_args and extra_link_args element by element.",
