      "omega-cpp publishes no call arguments at all and spans a callable on its declarator, not its body, so nothing written inside a function body or inside a PYBIND11_MODULE/TORCH_LIBRARY block can be joined to it: the individual m.def(\"forward\", &forward) registrations arrive only as call.method named def with no reachable owner and no argument text, and are not stated.",
      "the grammar bundle registers no cu or cuh extension, so CUDA kernel files are not parsed at all; a CUDA extension is recognised through the CUDA headers a parsed .cpp/.cc/.cxx/.hpp translation unit includes.",
